            {
              "id": "1d9e913f-c9ee-38b8-b1f2-e294f9bd4b79",
              "name": "## Description\n\nThis is a missing function-level access control issue. The view executes server-side actions and returns content based on request-controlled values, but it does not enforce authentication or authorization before calling sensitive logic.\n\nIn Python web applications, every view that can trigger behavior, load privileged content, or expose internal functionality should verify the caller first. In the shown sink, the request can influence trigger selection and output rendering, and the code invokes trigger_func(user_input) before any access check. That allows unauthenticated users, or authenticated users without the required role, to reach functionality that should be restricted.\n\nApply access control at the entry point of the view and validate permissions before dispatching any trigger function. Restrict the allowed trigger names to a safe allowlist, avoid executing user-selected functionality unless the current user is authorized for it, and return an explicit forbidden response when access is not permitted.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nRequire authentication on the view and enforce authorization before any business logic runs. In Django, use login_required for authenticated access and permission_required or explicit request.user.has_perm checks for role-based restrictions. Do not rely on hidden routes, client-side checks, or naming conventions as protection.\n\nTreat request parameters used to select code paths as untrusted. Replace dynamic function dispatch with a fixed allowlist of permitted actions, and map each action to a permission. Deny by default when the action is missing, unknown, or not authorized. Keep authorization checks close to the view and repeat them in deeper service layers for sensitive operations.\n\nAlso ensure output is rendered safely. Prefer template rendering with context variables so autoescaping applies, and explicitly escape any user input appended to HTML. This prevents the access control fix from leaving behind secondary injection risks in the same code path.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom django.contrib.auth.decorators import login_required, permission_required\nfrom django.http import HttpResponseForbidden\nfrom django.template.loader import render_to_string\nfrom django.utils.html import escape\nfrom rest_framework.response import Response\n\nALLOWED_TRIGGERS = {\n    \"safe\": get_trigger(name=\"example\", trigger=\"safe\")\n}\n\n@login_required\n@permission_required(\"app.can_view_secure_page\", raise_exception=True)\ndef _view(request):\n    user_input = _get_user_input(request)\n    trigger = request.GET.get(\"trigger\", \"safe\")\n    name = request.GET.get(\"name\", \"default\")\n\n    trigger_func = ALLOWED_TRIGGERS.get(trigger)\n    if trigger_func is None:\n        return HttpResponseForbidden(\"Forbidden\")\n\n    if not request.user.has_perm(\"app.can_execute_trigger\"):\n        return HttpResponseForbidden(\"Forbidden\")\n\n    trigger_func(user_input)\n\n    context = {\"user_input\": user_input}\n    template = render_to_string(f\"{name}.html\", context=context, request=request)\n\n    if name == \"xss\" and trigger == \"raw\":\n        template += \"<p>XSS: \" + escape(user_input) + \"</p>\"\n\n    return Response(template)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\nDjango\n djangorestframework\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/www-community/Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP Authorization Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-862: Missing Authorization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/862.html)\n- [Django authentication system](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/auth/default/)\n",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "```python\n# vulnerable_app.py\nfrom typing import Callable, Dict\n\n\nclass Request:\n    def __init__(self, params: Dict[str, str], user=None):\n        self.GET = params\n        self.user = user  # ignored: missing access control\n\n\nclass Response:\n    def __init__(self, body: str):\n        self.body = body\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        return self.body\n\n\ndef _get_user_input(request: Request) -> str:\n    return request.GET.get(\"input\", \"\")\n\n\ndef get_template(name: str) -> str:\n    templates = {\n        \"admin.html\": \"<h1>Admin panel</h1>\",\n        \"xss.html\": \"<h1>XSS demo</h1>\",\n        \"default.html\": \"<h1>Default page</h1>\",\n    }\n    return templates.get(name, \"<h1>Missing template</h1>\")\n\n\ndef dump_secrets(user_input: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"[SENSITIVE ACTION] dumping internal config for: {user_input}\")\n\n\ndef get_trigger(name: str, trigger: str) -> Callable[[str], None] | None:\n    triggers = {\n        (\"admin\", \"dump\"): dump_secrets,\n        (\"xss\", \"raw\"): lambda s: print(f\"[raw trigger] {s}\"),\n    }\n    return triggers.get((name, trigger))\n\n\ndef _view(request: Request) -> Response:\n    name = request.GET.get(\"name\", \"default\")\n    trigger = request.GET.get(\"trigger\", \"safe\")\n    user_input = _get_user_input(request)\n    trigger_func = get_trigger(name, trigger)\n\n    if trigger_func:\n        trigger_func(user_input)  # vulnerable sink: runs before authz\n\n    template = get_template(\"{}.html\".format(name))\n\n    if name == \"xss\" and trigger == \"raw\":\n        template += \"<p>XSS: \" + user_input + \"</p>\"\n\n    return Response(template)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(\"== Unauthenticated attacker reaches privileged action ==\")\n    req1 = Request(\n        {\"name\": \"admin\", \"trigger\": \"dump\", \"input\": \"exfiltrate-now\"},\n        user=None,\n    )\n    print(_view(req1))\n\n    print(\"\\n== Unauthenticated attacker also controls rendered output ==\")\n    req2 = Request(\n        {\"name\": \"xss\", \"trigger\": \"raw\", \"input\": \"<script>alert(1)</script>\"},\n        user=None,\n    )\n    print(_view(req2))\n```\n\n```text\n$ python vulnerable_app.py\n== Unauthenticated attacker reaches privileged action ==\n[SENSITIVE ACTION] dumping internal config for: exfiltrate-now\n<h1>Admin panel</h1>\n\n== Unauthenticated attacker also controls rendered output ==\n[raw trigger] <script>alert(1)</script>\n<h1>XSS demo</h1><p>XSS: <script>alert(1)</script></p>\n```\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"vulnerable-access-control-demo\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.10\"\ndependencies = []\n```"
