              "id": "2fed86ac-adca-3d48-8012-53f291ab291e",
              "name": "## Description\n\nThis issue is missing function-level access control. The Python view can be reached without enforcing authentication or authorization before it processes request data, invokes behavior selected at runtime, and returns content to the client.\n\nIn the shown sink, the handler reads user input, resolves a trigger function, and conditionally executes it, yet there is no access check on the view itself. That allows unauthenticated users, or authenticated users without the right privileges, to access functionality that should be restricted. In a Django-style application, access control should be applied at the view boundary so requests are rejected before any sensitive logic runs.\n\nThe fix is to require login and enforce an explicit permission or role check on the view. Apply the decorators directly to the handler, fail closed when the user lacks permission, and keep authorization decisions independent from request parameters such as name or trigger.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nProtect every non-public Python view with authentication and server-side authorization checks. In Django, use login_required for identity enforcement and permission_required or request.user.has_perm(...) for authorization. Reject requests before reading sensitive parameters, invoking action handlers, or rendering protected content.\n\nUse deny-by-default rules and map permissions to concrete business actions instead of trusting route names, query parameters, or UI visibility. If access depends on the target resource, perform object-level authorization inside the view after loading the resource and before executing any action. Also review dynamically selected functions such as get_trigger(name, trigger) to ensure only explicitly allowed operations are reachable by authorized users.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom django.contrib.auth.decorators import login_required, permission_required\nfrom django.http import HttpResponse, HttpResponseForbidden\n\n@login_required\n@permission_required('app.view_trigger', raise_exception=True)\ndef _view(request):\n    name = request.GET.get('name', '')\n    trigger = request.GET.get('trigger', '')\n    user_input = _get_user_input(request)\n\n    trigger_func = get_trigger(name, trigger)\n    if trigger_func:\n        trigger_func(user_input)\n\n    template = get_template(\"{}.html\".format(name))\n\n    if name == \"xss\" and trigger == \"raw\":\n        template += \"<p>XSS: \" + user_input + \"</p>\"\n\n    return HttpResponse(template)\n\n# If object- or role-specific authorization is required, enforce it explicitly:\n@login_required\ndef protected_view(request):\n    if not request.user.has_perm('app.view_trigger'):\n        return HttpResponseForbidden('Forbidden')\n\n    return _view(request)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\nDjango\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10: Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A5_2017-Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP Authorization Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Authentication Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authentication_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-306: Missing Authentication for Critical Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/306.html)\n- [Django authentication system](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/auth/default/)\n- [Django view decorators](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/http/decorators/)\n",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "```python\n# vuln_demo.py\nfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs\n\n\nclass Request:\n    def __init__(self, query_string: str, user=None):\n        self.GET = {k: v[0] for k, v in parse_qs(query_string).items()}\n        self.user = user  # unused: demonstrates missing access control\n\n\ndef HttpResponse(body: str) -> str:\n    return body\n\n\ndef _get_user_input(request: Request) -> str:\n    return request.GET.get(\"input\", \"\")\n\n\ndef get_template(name: str) -> str:\n    return f\"<html><body><h1>{name}</h1>\"\n\n\ndef dangerous_log(data: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"[triggered] dangerous action on: {data}\")\n\n\ndef get_trigger(name: str, trigger: str):\n    triggers = {\n        (\"admin\", \"log\"): dangerous_log,\n        (\"xss\", \"raw\"): lambda s: print(f\"[triggered] raw mode: {s}\"),\n    }\n    return triggers.get((name, trigger))\n\n\n# Vulnerable sink: no authentication/authorization before sensitive logic\ndef _view(request: Request):\n    name = request.GET.get(\"name\", \"\")\n    trigger = request.GET.get(\"trigger\", \"\")\n    user_input = _get_user_input(request)\n    trigger_func = get_trigger(name, trigger)\n\n    if trigger_func:\n        trigger_func(user_input)\n\n    template = get_template(\"{}.html\".format(name))\n\n    if name == \"xss\" and trigger == \"raw\":\n        template += \"<p>XSS: \" + user_input + \"</p>\"\n\n    return HttpResponse(template + \"</body></html>\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    print(\"Unauthenticated request reaches protected behavior:\")\n    req1 = Request(\"name=admin&trigger=log&input=delete_all\", user=None)\n    print(_view(req1))\n\n    print(\"\\nUnauthenticated request triggers reflected content:\")\n    req2 = Request(\"name=xss&trigger=raw&input=<script>alert(1)</script>\", user=None)\n    print(_view(req2))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n```text\n# requirements.txt\n# No external dependencies required for this console reproduction.\n```\n\n**Run**\n```bash\npython vuln_demo.py\n```\n\n**What it shows**\n- The view is callable by an unauthenticated user.\n- Request parameters select runtime behavior via `get_trigger(name, trigger)`.\n- Sensitive logic runs before any access check.\n- Client-visible content is returned afterward, matching the vulnerable sink pattern."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [],
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
