            {
              "id": "8f69c26e-7711-3f75-90bf-2954da075ed7",
              "name": "## Description\n\nUnsafe XML parsing can expose Python applications to XML external entity expansion, entity-based denial of service, and related parser attacks when untrusted XML is processed. In this case, parsing attacker-controlled data with lxml.etree.parse allows dangerous XML features to be interpreted unless the parser is explicitly hardened.\n\nFor the sink shown, replace direct parsing of untrusted input with a hardened XML parser that disables entity resolution and network access. In Python, a common fix is to use defusedxml.lxml.parse for untrusted XML so hostile payloads are rejected before they can read local files, trigger outbound requests, or consume excessive resources.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nDo not pass untrusted XML directly to lxml.etree.parse with default behavior. Use a hardened parser for all externally supplied XML, and ensure external entities, DTD processing, and network retrieval are not permitted. Keep XML parsing isolated to a small utility function so secure defaults are applied consistently.\n\nIf lxml must be used directly, construct an XMLParser with resolve_entities=False and no_network=True, and avoid features that load DTDs or fetch remote resources. Also validate input size and complexity to reduce denial-of-service risk from deeply nested or highly expanded documents.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom io import StringIO\nfrom defusedxml.lxml import parse\n\ndef parse_untrusted_xml(xml: str):\n    tree = parse(StringIO(xml))\n    return tree\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\ndefusedxml>=0.7.1\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP: XML External Entity (XXE) Processing](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/XML_External_Entity_(XXE)_Processing)\n- [CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html)\n- [defusedxml on PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/)\n- [lxml Parsing and Validation Documentation](https://lxml.de/parsing.html)\n",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "```python\n# vulnerable_xxe_demo.py\nfrom io import StringIO\nfrom lxml import etree\n\n# Reproducible vulnerable sink:\n# tree = lxml.etree.parse(StringIO(xml))\n\ndef parse_xml(xml: str):\n    tree = etree.parse(StringIO(xml))\n    return tree\n\ndef main():\n    # Reads local file content via external entity expansion.\n    # On Linux/macOS this targets /etc/hostname.\n    # Change to file:///C:/Windows/win.ini on Windows if desired.\n    xml = \"\"\"<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE data [\n  <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM \"file:///etc/hostname\">\n]>\n<data>&xxe;</data>\n\"\"\"\n    try:\n        tree = parse_xml(xml)\n        print(\"Parsed root text:\")\n        print(tree.getroot().text)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Parsing failed: {e}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"vulnerable-xxe-demo\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\ndependencies = [\n  \"lxml>=4.9.0\",\n]\n```\n\n```bash\npython vulnerable_xxe_demo.py\n```\n\nExpected behavior: if the environment permits entity resolution, the app may print the contents of the referenced local file, demonstrating unsafe parsing of attacker-controlled XML at this sink:\n\n```python\ntree = etree.parse(StringIO(xml))\n```\n\nFor a safe variant, use `defusedxml.lxml.parse` or a hardened `XMLParser(resolve_entities=False, no_network=True)`."
