          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nThis is a missing function-level access control issue. In Python web applications, a route handler that is exposed without authentication or authorization checks can be invoked by any client that can reach the endpoint.\n\nIn the shown aiohttp-style route, the GET handler for \"/\" immediately redirects the request to another path without first verifying the caller's identity or permissions. If this endpoint is intended for authenticated users, an attacker can access it directly and reach application flows that should be restricted. The fix is to enforce authentication before serving or redirecting the request and return an appropriate HTTP error when access is not allowed.\n\nApply access control at the route boundary and keep the check server-side. If different users have different privileges, validate both that the user is logged in and that the user is allowed to use this specific handler before issuing the redirect.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nRequire authentication and authorization checks in every handler that serves protected functionality, including routes that only redirect. In aiohttp applications, perform the check at the start of the view or enforce it centrally with middleware so unauthenticated requests never reach sensitive handlers. Use deny-by-default behavior, return 401 for unauthenticated users and 403 for authenticated users without permission, and avoid relying on client-side controls or hidden links as protection. Keep authorization rules mapped to roles or permissions and verify them on every request to the target route.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom aiohttp import web\n\nroutes = web.RouteTableDef()\n\ndef get_current_user(request):\n    return request.get(\"user\")\n\n@routes.get(\"/\")\nasync def index(request):\n    user = get_current_user(request)\n    if user is None:\n        raise web.HTTPUnauthorized()\n\n    if not user.get(\"can_access_index\", False):\n        raise web.HTTPForbidden()\n\n    raise web.HTTPFound(\"/vulnpy\")\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\naiohttp\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/www-community/Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP Authorization Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-306: Missing Authentication for Critical Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/306.html)\n- [CWE-862: Missing Authorization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/862.html)\n"
          },
