        {
          "ruleId": "a6c0f725-7a7c-384a-8971-38a555276301",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nImproper output encoding in server-side templates can lead to cross-site scripting. In Python, creating a Jinja2 Environment without enabling autoescaping allows template variables to be rendered directly into HTML, which can expose users to injected script content when untrusted data reaches the template.\n\nThe shown sink creates a Jinja2 Environment with only a loader, so HTML escaping is left disabled by default. For templates that render HTML, XML, or similar markup, configure the environment with automatic escaping enabled. In Jinja2, the recommended approach is select_autoescape so escaping is applied based on template file type and disabled for non-markup templates where it is not appropriate.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nEnable Jinja2 autoescaping for HTML and XML template rendering at environment creation time instead of relying on developers to remember manual escaping in every template. Prefer select_autoescape so markup templates are escaped by default while non-HTML templates can remain unaffected.\n\nKeep untrusted data in template variables rather than concatenating it into raw HTML. Avoid marking content as safe unless it has been explicitly sanitized for the target context. Review templates for uses of the safe filter, direct HTML construction, inline JavaScript, and attribute injection, because autoescaping reduces risk but does not make every output context safe automatically.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader, select_autoescape\n\nloader = FileSystemLoader(\"templates\")\nenvironment = Environment(\n    loader=loader,\n    autoescape=select_autoescape(\n        enabled_extensions=(\"html\", \"htm\", \"xml\"),\n        default_for_string=True,\n        default=False,\n    ),\n)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\njinja2\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Cross Site Scripting (XSS)](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/xss/)\n- [OWASP Cross Site Scripting Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [Jinja2 Environment API](https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/api/#jinja2.Environment)\n- [Jinja2 select_autoescape API](https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/api/#jinja2.select_autoescape)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/flask_app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 11,
                  "startColumn": 15,
                  "endLine": 11,
                  "endColumn": 41,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "environment = Environment(loader=loader)\n"
                  },
                  "sourceLanguage": "python"
                },
                "contextRegion": {
                  "startLine": 10,
                  "endLine": 12,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "loader = FileSystemLoader(Path(__file__).parent / \"templates\" / \"jinja\")\nenvironment = Environment(loader=loader)\n\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "glog-pfp-ruleFileLineCode/v1": "50354233eff6151be3144298aeefb4adf2963128e4e2344b04fec335d6db4933",
            "glog-pfp-ruleFileCode/v1": "7caefd1f5d31a73be8692e76a5d318587acb9e5dbd808147d6becc04dab51238"
          },
          "fingerprints": {
