        {
          "ruleId": "f45791d9-3686-30da-8159-0abe1f3b671a",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nThis is an unsafe template output encoding issue that can lead to cross-site scripting in Python applications using Jinja2. Creating a Jinja2 Environment without autoescaping means values rendered through {{ ... }} are inserted into HTML as raw text, so attacker-controlled input can become executable markup or script in the browser.\n\nIn this sink, the Environment is created as environment = Environment(loader=loader) with no autoescape setting. For HTML or XML templates, configure the environment with Jinja2 autoescaping so variables are escaped by default during rendering. This is the correct fix at the environment construction point because it protects all templates loaded through that environment unless a template explicitly opts out.\n\nUse select_autoescape for file-based templates so HTML-like extensions are escaped automatically. If this environment is only used for HTML rendering, autoescape=True is also acceptable, but select_autoescape is the safer and more precise default for mixed template types.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nEnable autoescaping on every Jinja2 Environment that renders HTML, XML, or other browser-consumed markup. Prefer select_autoescape so escaping is tied to template type instead of relying on developers to remember per-template settings. Keep automatic escaping enabled by default and only mark content safe after it has been validated and intentionally sanitized for the exact output context.\n\nDo not disable autoescape globally to preserve formatting. If trusted HTML must be rendered, sanitize it first and then mark only that specific value as safe rather than weakening the entire environment. Review templates for direct insertion into JavaScript, CSS, URLs, and HTML attributes, because those contexts may require additional context-specific encoding beyond standard HTML escaping.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader, select_autoescape\n\nloader = FileSystemLoader(\"templates\")\nenvironment = Environment(\n    loader=loader,\n    autoescape=select_autoescape(\n        enabled_extensions=(\"html\", \"htm\", \"xml\"),\n        default_for_string=True,\n        default=False,\n    ),\n)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\njinja2\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [Jinja2 Environment API](https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/api/#jinja2.Environment)\n- [Jinja2 select_autoescape API](https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/api/#jinja2.select_autoescape)\n- [OWASP Cross Site Scripting (XSS)](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/xss/)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)\n"
          },
