          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nCross-site scripting in server-side template rendering. This code renders a Jinja template directly and passes request data into the template context. When template rendering is done outside Flask's standard rendering path, autoescaping can be configured incorrectly or bypassed, which increases the risk that untrusted input is inserted into HTML output without proper escaping.\n\nIn Python Flask applications, the safer pattern is to render HTML views with render_template() and store templates as .html files under the templates directory so Flask applies Jinja configuration consistently. For the shown sink, read the query parameter, pass it as template data, and return render_template() instead of calling template.render() directly. This keeps untrusted data as plain data in the template context and relies on Jinja's HTML escaping for output.\n\nIf any user-controlled value must appear in HTML, do not mark it safe and do not concatenate it into markup in Python code. Keep autoescaping enabled, use normal variable substitution in the template, and only allow trusted, sanitized HTML through a narrowly reviewed path.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nUse Flask's render_template() for HTML responses instead of invoking Jinja Template.render() directly. Place HTML templates in the application's templates directory with a .html extension so Flask and Jinja apply autoescaping for HTML output by default. Pass untrusted values as template variables, not as prebuilt HTML fragments.\n\nDo not disable autoescape, do not use the safe filter on request data, and do not build HTML with string concatenation in view code. If rich text input is a hard requirement, sanitize it with a well-maintained HTML sanitizer before rendering and allow only a minimal set of tags and attributes. Review templates for use of safe, Markup, or custom filters that may reintroduce unescaped output.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom flask import Flask, render_template, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(\"/template-xss/jinja\")\ndef template_xss_jinja():\n    user_input = request.args.get(\"user_input\", \"\")\n    return render_template(\"template_xss.html\", path=\"/template-xss/jinja\", user_input=user_input)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\nFlask\nJinja2\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Cross Site Scripting (XSS)](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/xss/)\n- [Flask Templating Documentation](https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/templating/)\n- [Jinja Template Designer Documentation - HTML Escaping](https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/templates/#html-escaping)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "apps/flask_app.py",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
