        {
          "ruleId": "9eb7c8b7-70e3-397f-91b1-7cc667f067f8",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nThis is a missing access control issue. The view function is exposed without an authentication or authorization check, so any caller who can reach the route may invoke it and receive the redirect response.\n\nIn Python web applications, access control is typically enforced at the view layer with framework security configuration or decorators. For a Pyramid-style view like this one, the handler should require an authenticated principal and, when appropriate, a specific permission before redirecting the user to the target location.\n\nFor the shown sink, protect the function with a permission requirement and configure an authorization policy so unauthenticated or unauthorized requests are denied before the view runs. This prevents direct browsing to the endpoint by users who should not have access.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nRequire authentication and authorization on every non-public endpoint, and deny access by default. In Pyramid, enforce access checks with view permissions and a configured security policy instead of relying on route obscurity or client-side controls. Define permissions such as view, edit, or admin based on the action being performed, map them to principals in an ACL or security policy, and ensure anonymous users do not inherit privileged access. If the endpoint is intended only for signed-in users, require an authenticated principal before executing the redirect. Also review other view functions for the same pattern and apply consistent route and permission configuration across the application.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom pyramid.httpexceptions import HTTPFound\nfrom pyramid.view import view_config\n\n@view_config(route_name=\"index\", permission=\"view\")\ndef index(request):\n    return HTTPFound(location=\"/vulnpy\")\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\npyramid\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10: Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/)\n- [OWASP: Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/www-community/Broken_Access_Control)\n- [CWE-306: Missing Authentication for Critical Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/306.html)\n- [CWE-862: Missing Authorization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/862.html)\n- [Pyramid Security](https://docs.pylonsproject.org/projects/pyramid/en/latest/narr/security.html)\n- [Pyramid View Permissions](https://docs.pylonsproject.org/projects/pyramid/en/latest/narr/viewconfig.html#view-permissions)\n"
          },
