        {
          "ruleId": "e1ae6064-ebac-38b2-99de-bd8b8e0969e8",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nThis issue is missing function-level access control. In Python web applications, a request handler that serves content without first verifying the caller's identity and permissions can expose pages or actions to unauthenticated or unauthorized users.\n\nThe shown aiohttp view returns rendered HTML directly and does not enforce authentication or authorization before generating the response. Protect this handler by checking the current user from the request context or session and rejecting requests that are not logged in or do not have the required role. Apply the same control consistently to all routes that should not be public.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nRequire authentication before executing the handler and perform an explicit authorization check for the resource or action being served. In aiohttp, enforce this with middleware or decorators so the rule is centralized and difficult to bypass. Return 401 when no authenticated principal is present and 403 when the principal lacks permission.\n\nDo not rely on route obscurity or client-side checks to protect views. Store the authenticated user or claims in the request during authentication middleware, validate them on every protected endpoint, and use deny-by-default rules for sensitive pages. Add tests that verify anonymous users are blocked and low-privilege users cannot access privileged views.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom aiohttp import web\nfrom jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader, select_autoescape\n\njinja_env = Environment(\n    loader=FileSystemLoader(\"templates\"),\n    autoescape=select_autoescape([\"html\", \"xml\"]),\n)\n\ndef require_authenticated(handler):\n    async def wrapped(request):\n        user = request.get(\"user\")\n        if user is None:\n            raise web.HTTPUnauthorized(text=\"Authentication required\")\n        return await handler(request)\n    return wrapped\n\n@require_authenticated\nasync def _root_view(request):\n    user = request[\"user\"]\n    if not user.get(\"can_view_root\", False):\n        raise web.HTTPForbidden(text=\"Forbidden\")\n\n    template = jinja_env.get_template(f\"{name}.html\")\n    content = template.render(user=user)\n    return web.Response(text=content, content_type=\"text/html\")\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\naiohttp\njinja2\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/www-community/Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP Top 10 A01:2021 – Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/)\n- [CWE-306: Missing Authentication for Critical Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/306.html)\n- [CWE-862: Missing Authorization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/862.html)\n- [aiohttp Web Server Quickstart](https://docs.aiohttp.org/en/stable/web_quickstart.html)\n"
          },
