        {
          "ruleId": "7a57629a-aea7-36d1-b1b5-a8cdfc47f885",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nMissing function-level access control. This view can be reached without enforcing authentication or authorization before executing sensitive behavior, which allows unauthenticated or underprivileged users to invoke server-side actions and receive rendered content.\n\nIn this Python aiohttp-style handler, the request is processed immediately, user-controlled values are read, and a dynamically selected function is called before any access check occurs. That pattern is especially risky because the reachable action depends on request data, so an attacker may trigger code paths that were intended only for trusted users. Protect the handler at entry, verify the user identity from the session or middleware-populated request context, and enforce an explicit role or permission check before calling the trigger function or returning the page.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nApply authentication and authorization before any business logic in every route handler, not only in the user interface. In aiohttp applications, populate the authenticated principal in middleware or session handling, then fail closed with HTTPUnauthorized or HTTPForbidden when the principal is missing or lacks the required permission.\n\nUse explicit permission checks tied to the action being performed rather than relying on route names, hidden links, or client-provided values. Avoid dynamically dispatching sensitive functions directly from request parameters unless the target is selected from a strict server-side allowlist and guarded by per-action authorization. Centralize reusable checks in middleware, decorators, or helper functions so new endpoints do not accidentally bypass access control.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom aiohttp import web\n\n\ndef require_authenticated_user(request):\n    user = request.get(\"user\")\n    if user is None:\n        raise web.HTTPUnauthorized(text=\"Authentication required\")\n    return user\n\n\ndef require_permission(user, permission):\n    permissions = set(user.get(\"permissions\", []))\n    if permission not in permissions:\n        raise web.HTTPForbidden(text=\"Insufficient permissions\")\n\n\nasync def _view(request):\n    user = require_authenticated_user(request)\n    require_permission(user, \"triggers:execute\")\n\n    name = request.match_info.get(\"name\", \"\")\n    trigger = request.match_info.get(\"trigger\", \"\")\n    user_input = _get_user_input(request)\n    trigger_func = get_trigger(name, trigger)\n\n    if trigger_func is None:\n        raise web.HTTPNotFound(text=\"Trigger not found\")\n\n    trigger_func(user_input)\n\n    template = get_template(\"{}.html\".format(name))\n    return web.Response(text=template, content_type=\"text/html\")\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\naiohttp\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/www-community/Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP Authorization Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-306: Missing Authentication for Critical Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/306.html)\n- [CWE-862: Missing Authorization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/862.html)\n- [aiohttp Web Server Quickstart](https://docs.aiohttp.org/en/stable/web_quickstart.html)\n"
          },
          "locations": [
