        {
          "ruleId": "917d64cb-c673-3bf6-ba2c-e13de68da33b",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nBroken access control in a Python view allows the handler to return content without first enforcing authentication or authorization. In this pattern, the function accepts a request and immediately renders a template response, so any caller who can reach the route may be able to access the page regardless of identity or role.\n\nFor a view like this, access checks should be applied before the response is generated. In Django REST framework, require authenticated users and, when appropriate, add role- or object-specific permission checks in the view itself. This ensures the endpoint is denied by default and only authorized requests can render the template.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nProtect every view that serves non-public data with explicit authorization rules, not just routing conventions. In Django REST framework, use permission_classes to require authentication and add per-view checks for roles, groups, or object ownership before returning a response. Prefer deny-by-default behavior so new endpoints are not exposed accidentally.\n\nIf a page is intended to be public, document that decision explicitly. Otherwise, centralize access control with shared permission classes, keep sensitive routes behind authentication middleware, and add tests that verify anonymous users and low-privilege users receive 401 or 403 responses as appropriate.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom rest_framework.decorators import api_view, permission_classes\nfrom rest_framework.permissions import IsAuthenticated\nfrom rest_framework.response import Response\nfrom rest_framework.exceptions import PermissionDenied\n\n\ndef user_can_view_root(user):\n    return user.is_staff\n\n\n@api_view([\"GET\"])\n@permission_classes([IsAuthenticated])\ndef _root(request):\n    if not user_can_view_root(request.user):\n        raise PermissionDenied(\"You do not have permission to access this resource.\")\n\n    return Response(get_template(f\"{name}.html\"))\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\ndjangorestframework\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/www-community/Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP Authorization Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-285: Improper Authorization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/285.html)\n- [Django REST framework Permissions](https://www.django-rest-framework.org/api-guide/permissions/)\n- [Django Authentication in Web Requests](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/auth/default/)\n"
          },
