          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nCommand injection in process execution. In Python, calling subprocess.Popen with shell=True passes the command through the system shell, which interprets metacharacters such as ;, &&, |, $, and backticks. If any part of the command string is influenced by external input, an attacker can execute additional commands, change command behavior, or access data outside the intended operation.\n\nFor this sink, the fix is to avoid the shell entirely and invoke the target program with an argument list. Passing a sequence with shell=False prevents shell parsing and keeps each argument as data. If the command includes user-controlled values, validate them against a strict allowlist and reject unexpected input before building the argument list.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nDo not build shell command strings from dynamic input. Use subprocess.Popen, subprocess.run, or related APIs with a list of arguments and keep shell=False. Prefer absolute executable paths so the intended program is launched consistently.\n\nIf external input must influence arguments, constrain it with strict validation such as an allowlist of accepted commands, flags, or formats. Reject shell metacharacters rather than attempting to escape them manually. When possible, replace shelling out entirely with Python standard-library functions that perform the same task without invoking an operating system shell.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nimport subprocess\n\nsafe_command = [\"/usr/bin/program\", \"--option\", user_value]\n\nprocess = subprocess.Popen(\n    safe_command,\n    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n    stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,\n    shell=False,\n    text=True,\n)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\nsubprocess\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Command Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n- [CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\n- [Python subprocess module documentation](https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html)\n- [Python Command Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/python-command-injection)\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
