        {
          "ruleId": "7f18b2d5-9d33-36bc-97ae-4aec5ba666e8",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nUnsafe deserialization of untrusted data. In Python, calling pickle.loads() on data derived from user input is dangerous because the pickle format can instantiate arbitrary objects and execute attacker-controlled code during deserialization.\n\nIn this sink, user_input is converted to bytes and passed directly to pickle.loads(), so any external caller who can influence that value can trigger remote code execution. For data received from users, APIs, cookies, message queues, or other untrusted sources, replace pickle with a safe serialization format such as JSON and validate the decoded structure before using it.\n\nIf object serialization is required for trusted internal data, only unpickle data created by your own application and protected with strong integrity controls such as authenticated encryption or a server-side signature. Do not use pickle, marshal, or shelve for attacker-controlled input.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nDo not deserialize untrusted input with pickle.loads, pickle.load, marshal, or shelve. Use JSON for untrusted data interchange, then validate the parsed value against the expected schema, types, required fields, and size limits before processing it. In Python, this typically means json.loads followed by explicit checks or model validation.\n\nWhen you must persist Python objects internally, keep pickle usage strictly limited to trusted data generated by the same application boundary, and protect serialized blobs against tampering with authenticated encryption or digital signatures. Prefer designing interfaces around primitive data types instead of serialized objects, and reject unexpected content early with clear exceptions.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nimport json\nfrom typing import Any\n\n\ndef load_user_input(user_input: str) -> Any:\n    data = json.loads(user_input)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected a JSON object\")\n    return data\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\njson\ntyping\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP: Deserialization of untrusted data](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Deserialization_of_untrusted_data)\n- [CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html)\n- [Python documentation: pickle](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pickle.html)\n- [Python documentation: json](https://docs.python.org/3/library/json.html)\n"
          },
