        {
          "ruleId": "29e0f4ac-9d48-38b4-ba48-b51dc9478d2c",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nDynamic code execution in Python can lead to code injection. Calling exec() on data that is constructed at runtime allows arbitrary Python statements to run with the privileges of the current process.\n\nIn this case, the sink is exec(code), which is unsafe if code can be influenced by users, files, environment variables, network input, or other untrusted sources. The safest fix is to remove exec() entirely and replace it with explicit program logic, such as a dispatch table of allowed operations or structured data parsing. If the goal is only to parse literals, use ast.literal_eval instead of executing code.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nDo not pass dynamic strings into exec(). Replace dynamic execution with explicit control flow, a dictionary of allowed commands, or normal function calls. Treat all externally influenced input as untrusted, even when it appears to contain only simple expressions.\n\nIf the application needs configuration or data, use safe serialization formats such as JSON and validate the parsed structure before use. If only Python literals must be parsed, use ast.literal_eval rather than exec(). Keep the set of permitted actions small and explicit, and reject anything outside that allowlist.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom ast import literal_eval\n\nALLOWED_ACTIONS = {\n    \"print_hello\": lambda: print(\"hello\"),\n    \"print_goodbye\": lambda: print(\"goodbye\"),\n}\n\ndef run_action(action_name: str) -> None:\n    action = ALLOWED_ACTIONS.get(action_name)\n    if action is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unsupported action\")\n    action()\n\ndef parse_literal(value: str):\n    return literal_eval(value)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\nast (Python standard library)\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Code Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Code_Injection)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n- [Python docs: exec()](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#exec)\n- [Python docs: ast.literal_eval](https://docs.python.org/3/library/ast.html#ast.literal_eval)\n"
          },
