          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nDynamic code execution via compile(). In Python, passing untrusted or partially trusted input into compile() creates executable bytecode from text, which can allow an attacker to inject and run arbitrary Python code when that code object is later executed.\n\nThe sink shown compiles the variable code in exec mode, which is specifically intended for statement blocks and therefore expands the impact beyond simple expression parsing. If code is influenced by external input, an attacker can craft payloads that execute system commands, access application data, or alter program behavior. The safest fix is to remove dynamic compilation for untrusted input and replace it with strict parsing, an allowlisted command dispatcher, or safe data deserialization depending on the actual feature requirement.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nDo not use compile(), eval(), or exec() on data that originates from users, requests, files, environment variables, or other mutable sources. Replace dynamic Python code execution with a safe alternative that matches the requirement: ast.literal_eval() for Python literals, json.loads() for JSON data, or an explicit allowlist that maps permitted command names to callable functions.\n\nIf the application must support a limited expression language, implement a parser that only accepts known-safe syntax and validates the parsed structure before evaluation. Keep executable logic in code, not in user-controlled strings. Where removal is not immediately possible, enforce strict input validation, isolate execution in a hardened sandbox, and minimize privileges, but these are compensating controls rather than a complete fix.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nimport ast\n\ndef parse_user_value(code: str):\n    return ast.literal_eval(code)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\nimport ast\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP: Code Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Code_Injection)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n- [Python docs: ast.literal_eval](https://docs.python.org/3/library/ast.html#ast.literal_eval)\n- [Python docs: compile()](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#compile)\n"
          },
