          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nVulnerability label: unsafe XML parsing of untrusted input.\n\nIn Python, parsing attacker-controlled XML with etree.fromstring can expose the application to XML external entity expansion, entity recursion, and related denial-of-service or file disclosure attacks, depending on parser behavior and configuration. The risk is triggered here because user_input is passed directly into an XML parser.\n\nFor this sink, replace the direct lxml parser call with a hardened parser from defusedxml so dangerous XML constructs are blocked by default. If XML from untrusted sources must be accepted, also validate the expected document structure and reject oversized or unexpected payloads before further processing.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nDo not parse untrusted XML with permissive default parsers. Use a hardened XML library that disables external entities, DTD-related attacks, and entity expansion hazards by default. Keep XML inputs small, enforce expected schemas or element allowlists, and fail closed when parsing errors occur. If lxml must remain in use elsewhere, ensure untrusted data paths are isolated and configured with secure parser settings rather than calling generic parsing helpers directly.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom defusedxml.lxml import fromstring\n\n\ndef parse_user_xml(user_input: str):\n    return fromstring(user_input)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\npip install defusedxml\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP: XML External Entity (XXE) Processing](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/XML_External_Entity_(XXE)_Processing)\n- [CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html)\n- [CWE-776: Improper Restriction of Recursive Entity References in DTDs](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/776.html)\n- [defusedxml on PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/)\n- [lxml.etree API documentation](https://lxml.de/apidoc/lxml.etree.html)\n"
