            "text": "## Description\n\nThis is an unsafe XML parsing issue. In Python, parsing untrusted XML with xml.dom.pulldom.parseString can allow XML-based attacks such as external entity expansion, entity expansion denial of service, and other parser abuse when hostile input is processed.\n\nThe sink shown calls pulldom.parseString(user_input) directly on untrusted data. That means an attacker can supply crafted XML that consumes excessive resources or triggers unsafe entity handling during parsing. Replace the standard-library parser call with the hardened defusedxml equivalent, or initialize defusedxml protections before using stdlib XML parsers so untrusted XML is handled safely.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nDo not parse attacker-controlled XML with Python standard-library XML parsers unless they have been explicitly hardened. For this sink, prefer defusedxml.pulldom.parseString as a drop-in replacement. If migration is not immediately possible, call defusedxml.defuse_stdlib() during application startup before any XML parsing occurs, and keep XML inputs as small and simple as possible. Also validate expected document structure after parsing and avoid enabling optional features that resolve external entities or process DTDs.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom defusedxml import pulldom\n\ndef parse_user_xml(user_input: str):\n    return pulldom.parseString(user_input)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\npip install defusedxml\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP: XML External Entity (XXE) Processing](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/XML_External_Entity_(XXE)_Processing)\n- [CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html)\n- [Python Documentation: XML vulnerabilities](https://docs.python.org/3/library/xml.html#xml-vulnerabilities)\n- [defusedxml on PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/)\n"
