          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\n\nThis is an unsafe XML parsing issue. In Python, calling xml.sax.parseString on untrusted input can allow XML-based attacks such as entity expansion denial of service, external entity processing, and other parser abuse depending on parser behavior and configuration.\n\nThe shown sink parses user-controlled XML directly with sax.parseString(user_input, ContentHandler()). For untrusted data, use the hardened parser provided by defusedxml instead of the standard library SAX entry point. That change keeps the SAX-style parsing flow while adding protections designed for hostile XML content.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nDo not parse attacker-controlled XML with the standard library SAX parser entry points. Replace xml.sax.parseString with defusedxml.sax.parseString for untrusted input, and apply the same rule to other XML modules in the codebase. If legacy code must continue using standard library XML parsers, initialize process startup with defusedxml.defuse_stdlib() before any XML parsing occurs, but prefer explicit use of defusedxml APIs at each call site. Also enforce input size limits and avoid accepting XML features your application does not need, especially DTDs and external entities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom defusedxml import sax\nfrom xml.sax.handler import ContentHandler\n\ndef parse_user_xml(user_input: str):\n    handler = ContentHandler()\n    return sax.parseString(user_input, handler)\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\npip install defusedxml\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [defusedxml Project Documentation](https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/)\n- [Python xml.sax Documentation](https://docs.python.org/3/library/xml.sax.html)\n- [OWASP XML External Entity Processing](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/XML_External_Entity_(XXE)_Processing)\n- [CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html)\n- [CWE-776: Improper Restriction of Recursive Entity References in DTDs](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/776.html)\n"
